## 1. Summary Tab Formulas

Create a new sheet called `Summary`. All references assume your cleaned data is on a sheet called `Clean` with data in rows 2–421 and columns G–P as we set up.

**Overall counts (put labels in A, formulas in B):**

```
A1: Total Rows          B1: =COUNTA(Clean!A2:A421)
A2: OK Rows             B2: =COUNTIF(Clean!P2:P421,"OK")
A3: Review Rows         B3: =COUNTIF(Clean!P2:P421,"REVIEW")
A4: Dup-Email           B4: =COUNTIF(Clean!M2:M421,"DUP-email")
A5: Dup-Name-Time       B5: =COUNTIF(Clean!N2:N421,"DUP-name-time")
A6: Superseded          B6: =COUNTIF(Clean!O2:O421,"SUPERSEDED")
```

**Park breakdown (starting at row 8):**

```
A8: Park Name           B8: Volunteers
A9: West Side           B9: =COUNTIFS(Clean!J2:J421,A9,Clean!O2:O421,"<>SUPERSEDED")
A10: North Park         B10: =COUNTIFS(Clean!J2:J421,A10,Clean!O2:O421,"<>SUPERSEDED")
A11: REVIEW             B11: =COUNTIFS(Clean!J2:J421,"REVIEW",Clean!O2:O421,"<>SUPERSEDED")
```

Add more park rows as needed. If you want it dynamic instead of manually listing parks, put this in A9 and drag down:

```
=IFERROR(INDEX(SORT(UNIQUE(Clean!J2:J421)),ROW()-8),"")
```

Then pair it with the COUNTIFS in column B.

