## 2. Unique Volunteer Count After Deduping

The logic: use email as the identifier when present, fall back to name. Build a helper column first (column Q on `Clean`):

```
Q1: VolunteerKey
Q2: =IF(TRIM(C2)<>"", LOWER(TRIM(C2)), LOWER(TRIM(B2)))
```

Fill that down to row 421. Then on `Summary`:

```
A14: Unique Volunteers
B14: =SUMPRODUCT(
       (Clean!O2:O421<>"SUPERSEDED") *
       (1/COUNTIFS(Clean!Q2:Q421, Clean!Q2:Q421, Clean!O2:O421, "<>SUPERSEDED"))
     )
```

This counts each unique key exactly once among non-superseded rows. If you have any completely blank keys (no email and no name), add a REVIEW flag for those rows instead, since they can't be deduped reliably.

